## Advance, revisit, pause, and escalate

Advance after teach commits two distinct qualifying full passes; initial acquisition and delayed retention remain separate observations. After one failure, score, explain the named repair and use another unused item. After two unsuccessful independent attempts, pause repeated quizzing and revisit the explanation or diagnostic dependency. Source conflict stops the affected lesson and goes to ingest with the exact note heading. Missing or ambiguous keys, unsupported alternatives and an exhausted bank go to plan as plan_issue with 2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Financial_Markets_Instruments_I, O013, revision2/O013-C1, P004/V003/ingestion3 and the exact item ID. Closing a partial session does not fabricate acquisition.

## Answer-free recall handoff

Topic: Derive implied repo rates and choose a comparable eligible cheapest-to-deliver bond. Instruction: Begin a closed-note review with teach for O013; request an unused prepared delayed item before recap. Lesson: [[03_Agents/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Financial_Markets_Instruments_I/lessons/O013.md#Immediate and delayed checks]]. Teach supplies committed evidence and timestamps; recall alone assigns due dates or Todoist tasks. Deadline/retention horizon is null; this plan defines no learner result.

## Content provenance and generation boundaries

The complete checked-note passages above are reused with only heading-depth adaptation; exact origins and fingerprints are in source_manifest.md. Existing plan-created hypothetical exercises and their full keys are retained from P003; their algebra instantiates the included checked definitions. No new external academic claims are introduced. All figures retain checked vault-relative asset paths, captions and source qualifications. Main examples and assessment routes are fully prepared here.

Preserved assessment contract: only the named prepared full-capability items and six routes may establish acquisition or delayed evidence. Additional verified examples or practice may support explanation but cannot replace a named full check or reassessment gate. Teach may accept an independently verified equivalent method meeting the same pre-answer components and conditions. Ambiguous criteria or an exhausted fresh bank return to plan. The current objective revision is 2; unchanged item/criterion versions remain those explicitly stated above.
